+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+# MOD4 ONNX + MuJoCo 一键检查与驾驶启动器
+
+这个包把 4090 目标机上保留完好的 `model_16295.pt` 导出成 ONNX，并接到本机的闭链 MOD4 MuJoCo 模型。双击 `启动器.bat` 可导入新的 ONNX、自动校验并启动驾驶；`run_wasd.bat` 仍可直接启动包内默认策略。
+
+## 为什么选 model_16295
+
+- 主策略：`policies/mod4_general_16295.onnx`，源迭代 16295，检查点 SHA256 `d15aa478778b2985c434106b12b86f1eed556edbaff457d22e8817678f036e22`。
+- 4090 上正式评测记录显示它是完整五阶段链的最终策略：小陀螺 0.750、上台阶 0.750、下坡/下台阶 1.000。
+- `model_399.pt` 是后续未跑完课程的检查点，狗洞评测 0/64，并有技能退化；只作为按 `Tab` 切换的 A/B 对照，不称为成熟策略。
+- 2026-09-13 16:31 的新训练停在 model_150，成熟度不足，没有替换主策略。
+
+## 快速开始
+
+1. 双击 `启动器.bat`（英文入口为 `ONNX_MuJoCo_Launcher.bat`）。启动器使用 Windows 自带的 WinForms，不依赖 Python 的 Tk 组件。
+2. 点击“导入 ONNX”，选择训练机导出的策略。也可以把 ONNX 文件拖到 `启动器.bat` 上。
+3. 启动器会检查输入 `observation[*,35]`、输出 `action[*,6]`、零观测推理、SHA256、执行器数和闭链约束；通过后点“一键启动 MuJoCo”。
+4. 如果提示缺少 Python 包，先双击 `install_runtime.bat`。双击 `run_smoke_test.bat` 可做完整包冒烟检查。
+
+导入器会把外部策略复制到 `policies/imported/`，并同时复制同名 JSON 元数据（如果存在）。同名但内容不同的文件会自动追加哈希前缀，避免覆盖旧检查点。启动器显示的“PASS”只说明 ONNX 接口和 MJCF 机构能运行；策略是否训练成熟，需要在各测试场地观察直立、闭链误差、峰值力矩和通过能力。
+
+键位：
+
+| 键 | 功能 |
+|---|---|
+| W / S | 前进速度增加 / 减少 0.20 m/s |
+| A / D | 左转 / 右转角速度增加 0.50 rad/s |
+| X | 速度指令归零 |
+| Q / E | 车身高度降低 / 升高 10 mm，并切到手动模式 |
+| T | 自动地形模式开关 |
+| V | 循环手选 normal / stair / slope / recover / jump / height / state_time |
+| Y | 开关 MuJoCo 航向辅助，默认开 |
+| P | 施加 10 N、0.20 s 横向推力 |
+| R | 当前测试点复位 |
+| F | 循环传送到平地、台阶、斜坡、狗洞、起伏路、飞坡、中心岛、416 mm 挡墙 |
+| C | 当前策略和包内对照策略循环切换 |
+
+`Space`、`Tab`、数字键和 `F1..F8` 保留给 MuJoCo Viewer。这样 WASD 驾驶时可以继续使用 Viewer 的暂停、面板、可见组、帮助、信息、Profiler、传感器、全屏、坐标系和标签功能，不会一键触发两个动作。
+
+操控器默认开一个 80 `(rad/s)/(rad/s)` 的差速轮航向反馈，用来补偿 Isaac→MuJoCo 后实测的偏航漂移。它只修正两轮目标速度，ONNX 仍输出全部六个动作。按 `Y` 可以随时关闭，关闭后的结果就是原始策略适配器。
+
+## 模型和地图
+
+- `model/rm_training_arena.xml`：完整 277 件 CAD 外观、真实闭链拓扑、6 个主执行器、8 个可滚动导轮。
+- `model/rm_training_arena_headless.xml`：相同质量、惯量、碰撞、关节和闭链，只移除渲染网格，用于批量测试。
+- 控制频率 100 Hz，物理步长 0.5 ms；腿部位置环按训练运行参数 `Kp=2500, Kd=10`。
+- DM8009P 腿电机和 DM3519+15.8 轮电机都使用训练契约的转速扭矩包络和力矩上限。
+- 关节动作顺序固定为 `[left_crank, left_hip, right_crank, right_hip, left_wheel, right_wheel]`；硬限位投影约束 `crank - hip >= -1.0843 rad`。
+
+地图是面向手动驾驶的紧凑 RMUC2026 **训练特征地图**，包含 247.2 mm 狗洞、二级台阶、25°/12.1° 斜坡、飞坡与落地区、20--60 mm 起伏路、二级中心岛和二级顶面额外 50 mm 挡圈、416 mm 挡墙。它使用稳定的解析碰撞体，尺寸来自已交付 RMUC2026 地图数据；布局经过压缩，不是整场 CAD 三角网格的一比一复刻。
+
+## ONNX 验证
+
+导出图包含训练封装的 `[-6, 6]` 动作裁剪。使用 129 组零值、正态和均匀输入对比 PyTorch：
+
+| 策略 | ONNX SHA256 | ONNXRuntime 最大绝对误差 |
+|---|---|---:|
+| model_16295 主策略 | `9611637905617098458a63067cb96e2b3dd98e99f3541d329bbf6b768dc94f3b` | 2.62e-6 |
+| model_399 对照 | `f4bb4af9b46c3825ee13e09d706b1b4ff9a9ab8c664e35e5cf0d67fa754fd77b` | 2.38e-6 |
+
+每个 ONNX 旁的 JSON 记录完整 35 维观测布局、6 维动作顺序、源检查点和哈希。
+
+## 本机鲁棒性实测
+
+每条路线先跑 1 个标称回合，再跑 5 个独立随机回合。随机量包括：质量/惯量 ±10%、摩擦 ×0.8..1.2、阻尼 ×0.85..1.2、观测噪声 0..0.01、动作延迟 0..2 个控制周期，以及 10 N、0.1..0.3 s 横推。成功按每个回合独立判定，不跨复位累计。
+
+| 指标 | 原始 ONNX 适配器 | WASD 默认航向辅助 |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| 随机回合数 | 30 | 30 |
+| 机构/拓扑门禁 | 30/30 | 30/30 |
+| 保持直立 | 30/30 | 29/30 |
+| 严格路线成功 | 6/30 (20.0%) | 12/30 (40.0%) |
+| 平地前进 | 20% | 60% |
+| 倒车 | 0% | 80% |
+| 原地转向 | 100% | 100% |
+| 起伏路 / 台阶 / 狗洞 | 0% / 0% / 0% | 0% / 0% / 0% |
+| 最坏闭链残差 | 0.077 mm | 0.042 mm |
+
+完整逐回合证据在 `reports/robustness_report.json` 和 `reports/robustness_assisted_report.json`。
+
+这些结果说明 MJCF 机构和 ONNX 导出是稳定的，但这颗策略目前不能称为跨引擎鲁棒：原始适配器有明显偏航漂移；航向辅助改善手动平地驾驶，却没有补出起伏路、台阶和狗洞能力。狗洞标称回合在入口前仅前进约 0.78 m，发生 4 个控制周期的顶板接触，然后偏离通道。这个结论也与目标机上 model_399 的狗洞 0/64 相符。
+
+本报告是 MuJoCo sim-to-sim 测试，不是实车鲁棒性或安全放行证明。
diff --git a/build_assets.py b/build_assets.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b696436
--- /dev/null
+++ b/build_assets.py
@@ -0,0 +1,175 @@
+"""Build a self-contained MuJoCo scene around the corrected rolling MOD4 model."""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import copy
+import math
+import shutil
+import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
+from pathlib import Path
+
+
+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
+WORKSPACE = ROOT.parent
+SOURCE_XML = WORKSPACE / "chassis_mod4_work" / "folded_pose_sim" / "scene_tunnel_247p2_drive.xml"
+SOURCE_ASSETS = WORKSPACE / "chassis_mod4" / "assets"
+MODEL_DIR = ROOT / "model"
+
+
+def f(values) -> str:
+    return " ".join(f"{float(v):.9g}" for v in values)
+
+
+def add_box(world, name, full_size, pos, rgba, quat=None, friction=(0.9, 0.003, 0.0001)):
+    attrs = {
+        "name": name, "type": "box", "size": f([x / 2 for x in full_size]),
+        "pos": f(pos), "rgba": f(rgba), "contype": "1", "conaffinity": "2",
+        "friction": f(friction), "solref": ".0012 1", "solimp": ".99 .999 .0001",
+    }
+    if quat is not None:
+        attrs["quat"] = f(quat)
+    return ET.SubElement(world, "geom", attrs)
+
+
+def add_ramp(world, name, start_x, y, width, run, rise, direction, color):
+    angle = math.atan2(rise, run) * direction
+    length = math.hypot(run, rise)
+    # A thin box whose local +X follows the incline.  R_y(-angle) rises towards +X.
+    quat = (math.cos(angle / 2), 0.0, -math.sin(angle / 2), 0.0)
+    center_x = start_x + direction * run / 2
+    add_box(world, name, (length, width, 0.05), (center_x, y, rise / 2), color, quat)
+
+
+def add_field(world):
+    # Measured RMUC2026 dimensions used by the Isaac training map.  The layout is compact so it
+    # is practical to drive by hand, while each obstacle keeps its task dimension and collision.
+    ET.SubElement(world, "geom", {
+        "name": "arena_floor", "type": "plane", "size": "15 8 .1", "rgba": ".24 .27 .31 1",
+        "contype": "1", "conaffinity": "2", "friction": ".9 .003 .0001",
+        "solref": ".0012 1", "solimp": ".99 .999 .0001",
+    })
+    # Lane markings are visual-only and make navigation in the free camera easier.
+    for y, color in ((0.0, (.85, .75, .18, .5)), (-2.5, (.28, .65, .95, .35)),
+                     (2.5, (.30, .85, .45, .35)), (-4.8, (.95, .45, .22, .35)),
+                     (4.8, (.70, .45, .90, .35))):
+        ET.SubElement(world, "geom", {"name": f"lane_{str(y).replace('.', '_').replace('-', 'm')}",
+            "type": "box", "size": "14.5 .018 .001", "pos": f((0, y, .001)),
+            "rgba": f(color), "contype": "0", "conaffinity": "0", "group": "1"})
+
+    # 247.2 mm clear dog hole, 800 mm clear width, 300 mm deep.
+    tx, ty, depth, hole_w, hole_h, total_w = 1.5, 0.0, .30, .80, .2472, 1.50
+    side_w = (total_w - hole_w) / 2
+    wall_h = 1.00
+    add_box(world, "tunnel_left", (depth, side_w, wall_h),
+            (tx, ty + hole_w / 2 + side_w / 2, wall_h / 2), (.82, .30, .20, 1))
+    add_box(world, "tunnel_right", (depth, side_w, wall_h),
+            (tx, ty - hole_w / 2 - side_w / 2, wall_h / 2), (.82, .30, .20, 1))
+    add_box(world, "tunnel_roof", (depth, total_w, .18),
+            (tx, ty, hole_h + .09), (.90, .38, .22, 1))
+
+    # Two-step lane: 100/200 mm levels and mirrored descent.
+    sx, sy, run, width = -1.7, -2.5, .38, 1.35
+    for i, h in enumerate((.10, .20, .20, .10)):
+        add_box(world, f"stair_{i+1}", (run, width, h),
+                (sx + (i + .5) * run, sy, h / 2), (.34, .55, .78, 1))
+
+    # 25 degree climb, platform, and measured 12.1 degree descent.
+    ry, h = 2.5, .20
+    run_up = h / math.tan(math.radians(25.0))
+    add_ramp(world, "ramp_25_up", -2.0, ry, 1.35, run_up, h, +1, (.30, .70, .43, 1))
+    px = -2.0 + run_up + .55
+    add_box(world, "ramp_platform", (1.1, 1.35, h), (px, ry, h / 2), (.34, .63, .43, 1))
+    run_down = h / math.tan(math.radians(12.1))
+    add_ramp(world, "ramp_12_down", px + .55, ry, 1.35, run_down, h, -1, (.36, .68, .46, 1))
+
+    # Fly-ramp lane.  The arena floor is the 180 mm-deep bottom and the banks define the gap.
+    fy, bank_h = -4.8, .18
+    add_box(world, "fly_bank_before", (3.0, 1.35, bank_h), (-3.3, fy, bank_h / 2), (.62, .46, .28, 1))
+    launch_run = bank_h / math.tan(math.radians(20.0))
+    add_ramp(world, "fly_launch", -1.8, fy, 1.35, launch_run, bank_h, +1, (.84, .48, .20, 1))
+    landing_start = -1.8 + launch_run + .34
+    add_box(world, "fly_bank_after", (3.2, 1.35, bank_h),
+            (landing_start + 1.6, fy, bank_h / 2), (.62, .46, .28, 1))
+
+    # Continuous-looking rough lane from shallow 20--60 mm blocks.
+    bx, by = -4.8, 4.8
+    for i in range(12):
+        h = .02 + .02 * (i % 3)
+        add_box(world, f"rough_{i:02d}", (.30, 1.20, h),
+                (bx + i * .32, by, h / 2), (.58, .42 + .02 * (i % 3), .70, 1))
+
+    # Two-level centre island and the extra 50 mm ring on its upper deck.
+    ix, iy, l1, l2 = 5.0, 3.1, .18, .36
+    add_box(world, "island_level1", (2.0, 2.0, l1), (ix, iy, l1 / 2), (.42, .52, .60, 1))
+    add_box(world, "island_level2", (1.30, 1.30, l2), (ix, iy, l2 / 2), (.35, .47, .56, 1))
+    lip_h, lip_t = .05, .05
+    for name, size, pos in (
+        ("island_lip_n", (1.30, lip_t, lip_h), (ix, iy + .625, l2 + lip_h / 2)),
+        ("island_lip_s", (1.30, lip_t, lip_h), (ix, iy - .625, l2 + lip_h / 2)),
+        ("island_lip_e", (lip_t, 1.20, lip_h), (ix + .625, iy, l2 + lip_h / 2)),
+        ("island_lip_w", (lip_t, 1.20, lip_h), (ix - .625, iy, l2 + lip_h / 2)),
+    ):
+        add_box(world, name, size, pos, (.72, .44, .20, 1))
+
+    # Real-height 416 mm barricade used for avoidance / jump experiments.
+    add_box(world, "barricade_416", (.24, 1.60, .416), (5.0, -3.0, .208), (.72, .20, .18, 1))
+
+
+def build(headless: bool) -> Path:
+    tree = ET.parse(SOURCE_XML)
+    root = tree.getroot()
+    root.set("model", "MOD4 ONNX RMUC2026 manual arena" + (" headless" if headless else ""))
+    compiler = root.find("compiler")
+    compiler.set("meshdir", "assets")
+    visual = root.find("visual")
+    if visual is not None:
+        visual.find("global").set("azimuth", "145")
+        visual.find("global").set("elevation", "-24")
+    stat = root.find("statistic")
+    stat.set("center", "0 0 .3")
+    stat.set("extent", "8")
+    world = root.find("worldbody")
+    for geom in list(world.findall("geom")):
+        if geom.get("name") in {"ground", "tunnel_roof_247p2"}:
+            world.remove(geom)
+    chassis = world.find("body[@name='chassis']")
+    world.remove(chassis)
+    add_field(world)
+    # Spawn on the straight lane before the tunnel; user can teleport to other lanes.
+    chassis.set("pos", "-4 0 0.337742301121")
+    if not headless:
+        ET.SubElement(chassis, "camera", {"name": "follow", "mode": "trackcom",
+            "pos": "-2.5 -3 1.5", "xyaxes": ".75 -.66 0 .22 .25 .94"})
+    world.append(chassis)
+
+    if headless:
+        # Collision/inertia/topology remain identical; only 277 CAD render geoms and their mesh
+        # assets are removed.  This makes the randomized batch test load and step much faster.
+        for parent in root.iter():
+            for child in list(parent):
+                if child.tag == "geom" and child.get("class") == "visual":
+                    parent.remove(child)
+        asset = root.find("asset")
+        for child in list(asset):
+            if child.tag == "mesh":
+                asset.remove(child)
+
+    MODEL_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    out = MODEL_DIR / ("rm_training_arena_headless.xml" if headless else "rm_training_arena.xml")
+    ET.indent(tree, space="  ")
+    tree.write(out, encoding="utf-8", xml_declaration=True)
+    return out
+
+
+def main():
+    MODEL_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    dest_assets = MODEL_DIR / "assets"
+    if dest_assets.exists():
+        shutil.rmtree(dest_assets)
+    shutil.copytree(SOURCE_ASSETS, dest_assets)
+    shutil.copy2(SOURCE_XML, MODEL_DIR / "source_rolling_model.xml")
+    print(build(False))
+    print(build(True))
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    main()
diff --git a/drive_wasd.py b/drive_wasd.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9b98dc3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drive_wasd.py
@@ -0,0 +1,181 @@
+"""Interactive MuJoCo viewer for the exported MOD4 ONNX policy."""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import argparse
+from pathlib import Path
+import sys
+import time
+
+import mujoco
+import mujoco.viewer
+
+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
+sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))
+from sim_runtime import MODE_NAMES, Mod4Sim, RuntimeConfig  # noqa: E402
+
+
+SPAWNS = (
+    ("平地/狗洞", -4.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0),
+    ("二级台阶", -2.8, -2.5, 0.0, 0.0),
+    ("25度斜坡", -3.0, 2.5, 0.0, 0.0),
+    ("狗洞入口", 0.25, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0),
+    ("起伏路", -5.3, 4.8, 0.0, 0.0),
+    ("飞坡", -4.3, -4.8, 0.0, 0.18),
+    ("中心岛", 3.4, 3.1, 0.0, 0.0),
+    ("416mm挡墙", 3.4, -3.0, 0.0, 0.0),
+)
+
+# MuJoCo Simulate reserves Space, Tab, digits 0..5 and F1..F7.  Keep every
+# policy-control key away from that set so one keypress has exactly one effect.
+CONTROL_KEYS = {
+    "forward": (ord("W"), ord("w")), "reverse": (ord("S"), ord("s")),
+    "left": (ord("A"), ord("a")), "right": (ord("D"), ord("d")),
+    "stop": (ord("X"), ord("x")), "lower": (ord("Q"), ord("q")),
+    "raise": (ord("E"), ord("e")), "auto": (ord("T"), ord("t")),
+    "next_mode": (ord("V"), ord("v")), "push": (ord("P"), ord("p")),
+    "reset": (ord("R"), ord("r")), "yaw_assist": (ord("Y"), ord("y")),
+    "next_spawn": (ord("F"), ord("f")), "next_policy": (ord("C"), ord("c")),
+    "help": (ord("H"), ord("h")),
+}
+MUJOCO_DIRECT_RESERVED_KEYS = {32, 258, *range(ord("0"), ord("6") + 1), *range(290, 298)}
+assert not ({key for values in CONTROL_KEYS.values() for key in values} & MUJOCO_DIRECT_RESERVED_KEYS)
+
+
+HELP = """
+MOD4 ONNX / MuJoCo 键盘：
+  W/S  前进速度 +/−0.20 m/s       A/D  转向速度 +/−0.50 rad/s
+  X    急停速度指令               Q/E  车身高度 −/+ 10 mm
+  T    自动地形模式开关           V    循环手选任务模式
+  P    给车身一个 10 N 侧推       R    在当前测试点复位
+  Y    开/关 MuJoCo 航向辅助（默认开；补偿 Isaac→MuJoCo 的偏航漂移）
+  F    循环传送：平地、台阶、斜坡、狗洞、起伏路、飞坡、中心岛、挡墙
+  C    循环切换当前策略与包内对照策略
+  H    再显示本帮助               关闭窗口退出 MuJoCo
+
+Space、Tab、数字键和 F1..F8 保留给 MuJoCo Viewer，不再触发车辆命令。
+
+黄色=平地/狗洞，蓝色=台阶，绿色=斜坡，紫色=起伏路，橙色=飞坡。
+"""
+
+
+def main():
+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
+    parser.add_argument("--policy", type=Path, default=ROOT / "policies" / "mod4_general_16295.onnx")
+    parser.add_argument("--model", type=Path, default=ROOT / "model" / "rm_training_arena.xml")
+    parser.add_argument("--yaw-assist", type=float, default=80.0,
+                        help="MuJoCo yaw-rate feedback gain; use 0 for the raw ONNX policy")
+    parser.add_argument("--spawn", choices=[f"f{i}" for i in range(1, 9)], default="f1",
+                        help="initial test location")
+    args = parser.parse_args()
+    model_xml = args.model.resolve()
+    requested_policy = args.policy.resolve()
+    policy_candidates = [requested_policy,
+                         ROOT / "policies" / "mod4_general_16295.onnx",
+                         ROOT / "policies" / "mod4_tunnel_399_ab_only.onnx"]
+    policies = []
+    seen = set()
+    for path in policy_candidates:
+        path = path.resolve()
+        if path.exists() and path not in seen:
+            policies.append(path)
+            seen.add(path)
+    selected = 0
+    sim = Mod4Sim(model_xml, requested_policy, RuntimeConfig(yaw_assist_gain=args.yaw_assist))
+    current_spawn_index = int(args.spawn[1:]) - 1
+    current_spawn = SPAWNS[current_spawn_index]
+    label, x, y, yaw, ground = current_spawn
+    sim.reset(x, y, yaw, ground)
+    print(HELP, flush=True)
+    print(f"当前策略：{requested_policy.name}", flush=True)
+    print(f"模型：{model_xml.name}；初始位置：{label}", flush=True)
+
+    def status(prefix=""):
+        mode = MODE_NAMES[sim._auto_task()[0]] if sim.command.auto_mode else MODE_NAMES[sim.command.mode]
+        print(f"{prefix} vx={sim.command.vx:+.2f} m/s  wz={sim.command.wz:+.2f} rad/s  "
+              f"height={sim.command.height:.3f} m  mode={mode}  auto={sim.command.auto_mode}  "
+              f"yaw_assist={sim.cfg.yaw_assist_gain:g}", flush=True)
+
+    def key_callback(key):
+        nonlocal selected, current_spawn, current_spawn_index
+        if key in CONTROL_KEYS["forward"]:
+            sim.command.vx += .20
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["reverse"]:
+            sim.command.vx -= .20
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["left"]:
+            sim.command.wz += .50
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["right"]:
+            sim.command.wz -= .50
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["stop"]:
+            sim.command.vx = sim.command.wz = 0.0
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["lower"]:
+            sim.command.height -= .01
+            sim.command.auto_mode = False
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["raise"]:
+            sim.command.height += .01
+            sim.command.auto_mode = False
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["auto"]:
+            sim.command.auto_mode = not sim.command.auto_mode
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["next_mode"]:
+            sim.command.mode = (sim.command.mode + 1) % len(MODE_NAMES)
+            sim.command.auto_mode = False
+            print("手动任务模式：" + MODE_NAMES[sim.command.mode], flush=True)
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["push"]:
+            sim.push((0.0, 10.0, 0.0), .20)
+            print("已施加 10 N、0.20 s 横向扰动", flush=True)
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["yaw_assist"]:
+            sim.cfg.yaw_assist_gain = 0.0 if sim.cfg.yaw_assist_gain else 80.0
+            print(f"MuJoCo 航向辅助：{'开' if sim.cfg.yaw_assist_gain else '关'}", flush=True)
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["reset"]:
+            label, x, y, yaw, ground = current_spawn
+            sim.reset(x, y, yaw, ground)
+            print(f"已复位：{label}", flush=True)
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["next_spawn"]:
+            current_spawn_index = (current_spawn_index + 1) % len(SPAWNS)
+            current_spawn = SPAWNS[current_spawn_index]
+            label, x, y, yaw, ground = current_spawn
+            sim.reset(x, y, yaw, ground)
+            print(f"已传送：{label}", flush=True)
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["next_policy"]:
+            selected = (selected + 1) % len(policies)
+            from policy_runtime import OnnxPolicy
+            sim.policy = OnnxPolicy(policies[selected])
+            sim.last_action[:] = 0.0
+            print("当前策略：" + policies[selected].name, flush=True)
+        elif key in CONTROL_KEYS["help"]:
+            print(HELP, flush=True)
+        else:
+            # Leave MuJoCo Viewer shortcuts entirely to the Viewer.
+            return
+        sim.command.clamp()
+        status()
+
+    with mujoco.viewer.launch_passive(sim.model, sim.data, key_callback=key_callback,
+                                      show_left_ui=True, show_right_ui=False) as viewer:
+        viewer.cam.type = mujoco.mjtCamera.mjCAMERA_TRACKING
+        viewer.cam.trackbodyid = sim.chassis_id
+        viewer.cam.distance = 2.2
+        viewer.cam.azimuth = 145
+        viewer.cam.elevation = -22
+        next_tick = time.perf_counter()
+        next_report = next_tick + 2.0
+        while viewer.is_running():
+            sim.step_control()
+            viewer.sync()
+            next_tick += 1.0 / sim.cfg.policy_hz
+            delay = next_tick - time.perf_counter()
+            if delay > 0:
+                time.sleep(delay)
+            else:
+                next_tick = time.perf_counter()
+            if time.perf_counter() >= next_report:
+                h = sim.health()
+                print(f"t={h['time_s']:6.1f}s  xyz=({h['base_xyz'][0]:+.2f},"
+                      f"{h['base_xyz'][1]:+.2f},{h['base_xyz'][2]:.2f})  "
+                      f"upright={h['upright_cos']:.3f}  closure={h['closure_error_m']*1000:.3f}mm  "
+                      f"peak_tau={max(h['max_abs_torque_nm_actuator_order']):.2f}Nm",
+                      flush=True)
+                next_report += 2.0
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    main()
diff --git a/export_onnx.py b/export_onnx.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..374d3e1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/export_onnx.py
@@ -0,0 +1,127 @@
+"""Export rsl_rl actor checkpoints to deterministic, deployment-shaped ONNX.
+
+The checkpoint stores an ELU MLP under ``actor_state_dict``.  The exported graph
+accepts one or more 35-D policy observations and returns the action actually
+handed to the simulator, including the training wrapper's +/-6 clamp.
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import argparse
+import hashlib
+import json
+from pathlib import Path
+
+import numpy as np
+import onnx
+import onnxruntime as ort
+import torch
+from torch import nn
+
+
+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
+
+
+class Actor(nn.Module):
+    def __init__(self) -> None:
+        super().__init__()
+        self.mlp = nn.Sequential(
+            nn.Linear(35, 256), nn.ELU(),
+            nn.Linear(256, 128), nn.ELU(),
+            nn.Linear(128, 64), nn.ELU(),
+            nn.Linear(64, 6),
+        )
+
+    def forward(self, obs: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
+        return torch.clamp(self.mlp(obs), -6.0, 6.0)
+
+
+def sha256(path: Path) -> str:
+    h = hashlib.sha256()
+    with path.open("rb") as f:
+        for block in iter(lambda: f.read(1024 * 1024), b""):
+            h.update(block)
+    return h.hexdigest()
+
+
+def export_one(checkpoint: Path, output: Path, role: str) -> dict:
+    raw = torch.load(checkpoint, map_location="cpu", weights_only=False)
+    state = raw["actor_state_dict"]
+    model = Actor().eval()
+    missing, unexpected = model.load_state_dict(
+        {k: v for k, v in state.items() if not k.startswith("distribution.")}, strict=False)
+    if missing or unexpected:
+        raise RuntimeError(f"state mismatch: missing={missing}, unexpected={unexpected}")
+
+    output.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    dummy = torch.zeros(3, 35, dtype=torch.float32)
+    torch.onnx.export(
+        model, dummy, output, input_names=["observation"], output_names=["action"],
+        dynamic_axes={"observation": {0: "batch"}, "action": {0: "batch"}},
+        opset_version=18, do_constant_folding=True, dynamo=False,
+    )
+    onnx.checker.check_model(onnx.load(output))
+
+    rng = np.random.default_rng(20260913)
+    cases = np.concatenate([
+        np.zeros((1, 35), np.float32),
+        rng.normal(0.0, 0.5, (64, 35)).astype(np.float32),
+        rng.uniform(-3.0, 3.0, (64, 35)).astype(np.float32),
+    ])
+    with torch.no_grad():
+        expected = model(torch.from_numpy(cases)).numpy()
+    session = ort.InferenceSession(str(output), providers=["CPUExecutionProvider"])
+    actual = session.run(["action"], {"observation": cases})[0]
+    max_abs_error = float(np.max(np.abs(expected - actual)))
+    if max_abs_error > 2.0e-5:
+        raise RuntimeError(f"ONNX parity failed: max_abs_error={max_abs_error:g}")
+
+    meta = {
+        "schema_version": 1,
+        "role": role,
+        "source_checkpoint": checkpoint.name,
+        "source_checkpoint_sha256": sha256(checkpoint),
+        "source_iteration": int(raw.get("iter", -1)),
+        "onnx_sha256": sha256(output),
+        "onnx_opset": 18,
+        "onnxruntime_max_abs_error": max_abs_error,
+        "input": {"name": "observation", "shape": ["batch", 35], "dtype": "float32"},
+        "output": {"name": "action", "shape": ["batch", 6], "dtype": "float32", "clamp": [-6.0, 6.0]},
+        "observation_layout": [
+            {"slice": [0, 3], "name": "command_vx_vy_wz", "scale": 1.0},
+            {"slice": [3, 4], "name": "height_command_m", "scale": 5.0},
+            {"slice": [4, 7], "name": "base_angular_velocity_body_rad_s", "scale": 0.5},
+            {"slice": [7, 10], "name": "projected_gravity_body", "scale": 1.0},
+            {"slice": [10, 14], "name": "leg_position_relative_rad", "scale": 1.0},
+            {"slice": [14, 16], "name": "reserved_wheel_position", "constant": 0.0},
+            {"slice": [16, 20], "name": "leg_velocity_rad_s", "scale": 0.1},
+            {"slice": [20, 22], "name": "wheel_velocity_rad_s", "scale": 0.1},
+            {"slice": [22, 28], "name": "last_applied_action", "scale": 1.0},
+            {"slice": [28, 35], "name": "mode", "labels": ["normal", "stair", "slope", "recover", "jump", "height", "state_time"]},
+        ],
+        "leg_state_order": ["left_crank", "left_hip", "right_crank", "right_hip"],
+        "action_order": ["left_crank", "left_hip", "right_crank", "right_hip", "left_wheel_spin", "right_wheel_spin"],
+        "deterministic": True,
+    }
+    output.with_suffix(".json").write_text(json.dumps(meta, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
+    return meta
+
+
+def main() -> None:
+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()
+    parser.add_argument("--checkpoint", type=Path)
+    parser.add_argument("--output", type=Path)
+    parser.add_argument("--role", default="manual")
+    args = parser.parse_args()
+    if args.checkpoint:
+        jobs = [(args.checkpoint, args.output or ROOT / "policies" / (args.checkpoint.stem + ".onnx"), args.role)]
+    else:
+        jobs = [
+            (ROOT / "incoming" / "model_16295.pt", ROOT / "policies" / "mod4_general_16295.onnx", "recommended_general"),
+            (ROOT / "incoming" / "model_399.pt", ROOT / "policies" / "mod4_tunnel_399_ab_only.onnx", "ab_comparison_not_mature"),
+        ]
+    for checkpoint, output, role in jobs:
+        print(json.dumps(export_one(checkpoint.resolve(), output.resolve(), role), ensure_ascii=False))
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    main()
